# Opinion

Meeting: 0020-ensure-docker-deployment-uses-real-auth-for-web-client
Agent: ArchitectA
Task: ensure docker deployment uses real auth for web client
Context:
- Web client was defaulting to seed data even when deployed, with no enforcement of real auth or crypto guarantees.
- Containerized deployments lacked a runtime-config hook to inject issuer/client metadata and JWKS details.
Position:
- Enforce OIDC inputs (issuer, audience, endpoints, JWKS) as first-class requirements when sync is enabled; fail fast instead of seeding.
- Keep HTTPS-only everywhere except localhost to match the security spec, and require JWKS-backed verification before any remote state call.
Recommendations:
- Validate the `/state` PUT/GET contract against the live API; if the production surface differs, add a minimal adapter layer instead of loosening auth.
- Add a deployment smoke that exercises JWKS fetch + JWT verification to catch issuer or key-rotation drift before users see seed data again.
